# Per-Frame Apply Parity: VariationPipeline ↔ RandomizeFace ↔ LoadHeadData

Three operators share the same "apply to scene" responsibility. Any change to
what the pipeline applies per frame **must be evaluated** against both
`RandomizeFace` and `LoadHeadData`.

```
VariationPipeline  ──── inner loop body ────▶  RandomizeFace   (live random)
                                          ▶  LoadHeadData    (from snapshot)
```

## Per-Frame Apply Core (all three must stay in sync)

### Bones
- `_apply_transforms_to_bones(chaos_joints, transforms, frame)` — RandomizeFace
- `apply_bone_transforms(armature, snapshot["chaos_joints"], frame)` — LoadHeadData (snapshot equivalent)

### Blendshapes — applied to every object in this list
| Object | RandomizeFace fn | LoadHeadData fn |
|---|---|---|
| `head_mesh` | `_apply_weights_to_shape_keys` | `apply_shape_key_values` |
| `eye_wedge_R_obj` | `_apply_weights_to_shape_keys` | `apply_shape_key_values` |
| `eye_wedge_L_obj` | `_apply_weights_to_shape_keys` | `apply_shape_key_values` |
| `eye_wedge_R_bake` | `_apply_weights_to_shape_keys` | `apply_shape_key_values` |
| `eye_wedge_L_bake` | `_apply_weights_to_shape_keys` | `apply_shape_key_values` |
| `R_projector` | `_apply_weights_to_shape_keys` | `apply_shape_key_values` |
| `L_projector` | `_apply_weights_to_shape_keys` | `apply_shape_key_values` |
| `hd_eye_R` | `_apply_weights_to_shape_keys` | `apply_shape_key_values` |
| `hd_eye_L` | `_apply_weights_to_shape_keys` | `apply_shape_key_values` |
| `eyebrows_obj` | `_apply_weights_to_shape_keys` | `apply_shape_key_values` |
| `eyelashes_obj` | `_apply_weights_to_shape_keys` | `apply_shape_key_values` |

### Reset Frame
Both use the same list:
`reset_frame(chaos_joints, [head_mesh, eye_wedge_R_obj, eye_wedge_L_obj, eye_wedge_R_bake, eye_wedge_L_bake, R_projector, L_projector, hd_eye_R, hd_eye_L, eyebrows_obj, eyelashes_obj], frame)`

### Color
A single shared color is used for both body and eyes — there is no separate eye color.

| Step | RandomizeFace | LoadHeadData |
|---|---|---|
| Body color | `randomize_head_material_color(head_mesh, rng_color, frame)` | `apply_material_color(head_mesh, skin_color, frame)` |
| Eye color R | `assign_eye_color(eye_wedge_R_bake, cfg.projection.eye_wedge_R_bake_name, ...)` | same, using `skin_color` |
| Eye color L | `assign_eye_color(eye_wedge_L_bake, cfg.projection.eye_wedge_L_bake_name, ...)` | same, using `skin_color` |
| Attractive color | `apply_attractive_color(...)` if not None | ❌ intentionally absent — not applicable to loading |

## Intentional Differences (do NOT add to RandomizeFace or LoadHeadData)

| Feature | Pipeline-only or RF-only reason |
|---|---|
| FBX/blend import, scene setup, material append | Pipeline setup — runs once |
| Multi-frame `for frame in range(...)` loop | Pipeline iterates; single-frame ops use `frame_current` |
| `bpy.ops.wm.save_as_mainfile` | Pipeline batch checkpoint |
| Deterministic `_random.Random(cfg.runner.seed)` | Pipeline is reproducible; RandomizeFace is intentionally random |
| `generate_*` / attractor / constrain / flatten | RandomizeFace generates live; LoadHeadData reads from snapshot |
| `apply_attractive_color` | RandomizeFace only — not meaningful when restoring a fixed saved state |

## Checklist When Editing the Per-Frame Loop

- [ ] Added a new `_apply_weights_to_shape_keys` call in the pipeline? → Add it in **both** RandomizeFace and LoadHeadData, with matching ref lookups and error guards in each.
- [ ] Added a new `_apply_transforms_to_bones` variant? → Mirror in RandomizeFace; evaluate for LoadHeadData.
- [ ] Changed the `reset_frame` mesh list? → Keep all three lists identical.
- [ ] Changed attract / constrain / flatten call signatures? → Update RandomizeFace call site.
- [ ] Added a new tracked object ref? → Add `get_ref` + error guard to **both** RandomizeFace and LoadHeadData.
- [ ] Changed the color application (body or eye)? → Update both RandomizeFace and LoadHeadData; remember they use different source variables (`rng_color` vs `skin_color`).

## User Notification Requirement

Whenever `SYNTHHEAD_OT_RandomizeFace` **or** `SYNTHHEAD_OT_LoadHeadData` is
modified as a consequence of syncing with the pipeline — even if the user only
asked about the pipeline — you **MUST** call this out explicitly in your
response with a bold header for each operator touched, for example:

> **⚠️ RandomizeFace was also updated to stay in sync with the pipeline.**
> **⚠️ LoadHeadData was also updated to stay in sync with the pipeline.**

The user may not be expecting changes to these operators and must always be made
aware when they have been touched.
